{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["And the sense of <b>that we may preserve seed from our father</b> is perhaps that they said: Let us do the deed that is upon us to do, for perhaps Elohim will have compassion and we will give birth to male and female, and the world will be perpetuated through them, for 'the world is built by kindness' (Psalms 89:3), and HaShem did not save us for nothing. Now they were modest and did not wish to say to their father that he should marry them, for a son of Noah is permitted in his daughter (Sanhedrin 58b), or because the matter was exceedingly repugnant in the eyes of those generations and such had never been done. And likewise our Sages in the Aggadot greatly exonerate Lot (Nazir 23b)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:32:10.992415784Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}